            <ArticleTitle>[A nerve root anomaly with lumbar disc prolapse. Report of a case (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>293-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of sciatica with partial paralysis of both lower limbs is reported. At operation a prolapse of the L4/5 intervertebral disc on the right side was associated with an anomaly of the left fifth lumbar root which was lower and more horizontal than normal. The authors give a short review of the literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
